      "a": {
        "decoded_comment": [
          80
        ],
        "form_line": 26,
        "old": "The configuration half is `DOM-10`'s gate on the create's ordering capability (`DOM-16`):\n`API-7`'s step 5d at admission and `OPS-43`'s step 3 at claim."
      },
      "b": {
        "decoded_comment": [
          41,
          89
        ],
        "form_line": 35,
        "old": "\"In its provider\noptions\" until 2026-09-05, while `WIR-17` placed it at the top level; the wire contract wins, and a\nspending authorization nested inside a driver-private object is one a strict server could not tell\nfrom any other option."
      },
      "c": {
        "decoded_comment": [
          266
        ],
        "form_line": 212,
        "old": "While it is still queued and unclaimed, restart with a descriptor for that account that\n      removes only `list_offers`, keeping the ordering capability declared and the driver's\n      List offers code path answering, so the test proves the gate exists, as `CNF-19` does."
      },
      "d": {
        "decoded_comment": [
          77
        ],
        "form_line": 23,
        "old": "**PRV-10** For a paid create (`DOM-16`), create MUST reject the request unless the\nrequest carries an explicit purchase acknowledgement (`WIR-17`'s top-level\n`acknowledge_purchase`), *and* the account is configured to allow ordering."
      },
      "e": {
        "decoded_comment": [
          87
        ],
        "form_line": 33,
        "old": "**API-15** A paid create request (`DOM-16`) MUST carry an explicit purchase\nacknowledgement — `WIR-17`'s top-level `acknowledge_purchase`, which the wire contract\nowns — in addition to the account being configured to allow ordering (`PRV-10`)."
      }
    }
